<HelloFraandsPage updated="2026-10-28" title="Community guidelines" summary="Izzat se baat karein; har insaan ki hadon ka dhyaan rakhein." review={true} related={[{href:'/terms',label:'Terms of use'},{href:'/grievance',label:'Grievance redressal'}]}>
<p>These guidelines apply to conversations and account activity. Respect other people and use the available reporting controls when something goes wrong.</p>
<h2>What is welcome</h2>
<p>Adults aged 18 or older can talk to their favourite influencers over a private call and discuss a shared interest. Astrology and tarot are for reflection and entertainment, with no promised outcomes. Respect a person's decision to decline, end or change the topic.</p>
<p>With an influencer who lists women's health as a topic on their profile, everyday health experiences are a normal topic (see <a href="/women-only">women's safety</a>). Discussing periods, PCOS or pregnancy is not in itself sexual misconduct. Harassment is still reportable. Influencers must not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
<h2>What is not allowed</h2>
<ul><li>Abuse, gaali, threats, harassment or coercion.</li><li>Sexual or suggestive talk, and any adult services.</li><li>Selling anything on a call: products, services, courses or remedies. Influencers can sell through the {BRAND.name} Shop instead.</li><li>Financial tips, loans, investment or money-making schemes, and network marketing (MLM).</li><li>Asking for or taking payment outside {BRAND.name}. Never pay or get paid by UPI, bank transfer or cash outside the app.</li><li>Sharing or asking for phone numbers, UPI IDs, addresses, social accounts or other contact details, or arranging meetings.</li><li>Impersonation, false qualifications, or professional medical or legal advice.</li><li>Using the service under 18, sharing another person's private information.</li></ul>
<h2>How reports and strikes work</h2>
<p>Influencers can end a call with <strong>*</strong>, or use <strong>#</strong> to end, block the caller from that influencer and flag an incident. A block stops future contact with that influencer; it does not by itself prove misconduct or permanently ban an account.</p>
<p><strong>Every call is recorded for safety. Nobody listens live.</strong> After the call, an AI system turns the recording into text and checks it against these guidelines. Women-only calls are recorded and checked in the same way. Read what we keep, for how long and who can read it in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
<p>A report from a fan or an influencer also sends the call for a check. A report is only a report until it is reviewed. Mentions of self-harm go to welfare review and must never count as a strike.</p>
<h2>Strikes</h2>
<p>A strike is given for one call and one person, a fan or an influencer. When the AI is very sure a rule was broken, the strike can be given straight away. When it is less sure, our safety team looks first. The person gets a message that says what happened and how to appeal, and sees only their own words.</p>
<ul><li>A strike counts for <strong>90 days</strong>, then it expires.</li><li><strong>Three active strikes pause the account.</strong> A paused influencer is hidden, and calls, the queue and new bookings stop. Booked calls are cancelled and the fans get a full refund to their wallets. A paused fan cannot call or book but can still sign in and withdraw wallet money.</li><li><strong>Appeal once per strike.</strong> Reply APPEAL on WhatsApp, or tap Appeal in the app or on the website. A person reviews it. If it is accepted, the strike is removed.</li><li><strong>Only a person can ban an account.</strong> A ban is permanent and the phone number cannot be used to sign up again. Threats, sexual harassment, fraud or danger to someone can lead to a pause or an immediate ban.</li></ul>
<p>Blocking by three distinct influencers can freeze the caller account pending review; two calls ended with the influencer's # key within 24 hours can trigger a 24-hour suspension. These controls cannot guarantee that harm will be detected.</p>
<h2>Money when an account is paused or banned</h2>
<p>A paused influencer's earnings are held until our review ends. If a ban is confirmed, fans of the flagged calls are refunded first from the held money, and the rest is paid to the influencer's UPI ID as for a closed account. A banned fan can still sign in and withdraw wallet money with the Withdraw button. Minutes already spoken remain billable under the <a href="/wallet-terms">wallet terms</a>.</p>
<h2>On a call</h2>
<p>Spammy, sexual or threatening behaviour is not allowed. Do not share your phone number, UPI ID or address, and never pay outside {BRAND.name}; if someone asks, say no and report it after the call. You can end any call yourself, or press # to end the call and block the person. We never ask for OTP, UPI PIN, passwords or bank details; if anyone does, report them.</p>
<p>Influencers also follow the <a href="/hosts/rules">influencer rules</a>. See <a href="/report">Report a user</a> for reporting availability and <a href="/grievance">grievance redressal</a> for the published route to challenge account action. Reporting an incident does not guarantee a particular outcome.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
